libmarinholab-solver-osqp (26.10.00) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix CMake package config: the imported target is now created only
    when it does not exist, so calling find_package() more than once (a
    superbuild, or several components) no longer aborts with "another
    target with the same name already exists". Add the vendored OSQP
    with EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL so the package no longer ships libosqpstatic.a
    and cmake/osqp/, whose exported targets resolved find_package(osqp)
    from any other project on the machine onto this private copy; the
    OSQP and qdldl headers are installed by this project instead.

 -- Murilo M Marinho <murilomarinho@ieee.org>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:52:07 +0000

libmarinholab-solver-osqp (26.09.00) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian package of the C++ part of the solver-osqp project:
    the marinholab::solvers::osqp library (Solver + Configuration) and its
    OSQP dependency, built with CMake and -O3.
    The pybind11 Python extension is not packaged; it is built by
    `pip install .`.

 -- Murilo M Marinho <murilomarinho@ieee.org>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0100
